Z||000004||WKDFIRO||07-12-2000||03:03 PM||||The only problem with imports making 200+ hp (An astonishing feat given the almost nothing displacement they are running.) is that its mostly top end. Say what you must about "low tech" pushrods but we have the big shovel when it comes to digging up the low end torque. Granted the big shovel won't move air as fast on top end as well as the "small shovels" of the DOHC design but when you are at the stop light its all about low end torque.<P>I got to demonstrate this when I had just gotten my 2.5 inch exhaust put onto my 85 GT with a built 2.8 (yeah I know I wish I had known about the 3.4s...)I was waiting at a stop light on a hill and an MR-2 pulled up and must have seen the pipes and started tooting his own pipes too. Not only was I smoking 225/50 16 wheels up hill I walked away from him in second gear. He was still waiting for his engine to spool up.<P>Give me low end torque and watch me smile!||||reg||6
Z||000005||HYPTNOTiSE||07-13-2000||03:56 PM||||my buddy's 96 vtech TEG, runs 14.0's on street tires blowing em off through 3rd gear.  He's running a jackson racing charger with only 6psi boost.  Your opponent musta not known how to drive. If you race integra and he hits 3rd gear, just hang your arm out the window and wave, cos they will long gone real quick.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ nitrous||||reg||1
